                                "sense_id": "066c32b2-ef9b-3be4-9351-86cf21a2d9d8",
                                "text": "Cross moline sarcelled, or voided throughout, cross recercelée, or recersile, or recercelée voided or disjoined, which has also been called a cross fleury biparted. This is borne by the names of Knollys, or Knowles, and Verney. Gules, a cross moline sarcelled argent. BEC. […]"
